Found while auditing the error prose for #27, not fixed there (that ticket was scoped to the recipient message in the LIMITATIONS section).

lib/Crypt/Age.pm, =method decrypt:

    The method tries each identity against each recipient stanza in the header
    until one successfully unwraps the file key. Dies if no matching identity is
    found or if the MAC verification fails.

Nothing there is wrong, and both named modes are real. It is incomplete: decrypt also dies on an invalid version line, on a structurally invalid stanza, on payload authentication failure at a chunk, on an empty payload, and now on a ciphertext holding a code point above 0xFF (#26). =method decrypt_file and =method decrypt_filehandle already list the fuller set, so the three descriptions of the same failure surface disagree on length.

Worth aligning the three, or reducing decrypt to a reference to one of them, rather than maintaining three lists.

Audited and found current in the same pass, no action needed: the "No matching identity found" quote, the literal age-encryption.org/v1 version line claim, the unwrap_file_key X25519-only claim, and the encrypt_file / encrypt_filehandle / decrypt_file / decrypt_filehandle failure lists.
Aligned =method decrypt's failure list in lib/Crypt/Age.pm with decrypt_file/decrypt_filehandle (left unchanged, per audit). Verified every claim against code: Header::parse_from_fh (version line, stanza structure), Header::unwrap_file_key (no-match/MAC), Primitives::decrypt_payload_fh (chunk auth failure incl. empty payload), and the utf8::downgrade check in Crypt::Age::decrypt (#26). Reduced decrypt's dies-sentence to a reference to L</decrypt_file> instead of a third prose list, per the ticket's stated preference. prove -lr t/ green: 8 files, 574 tests, incl. t/04-interop.t against age 1.2.1 + rage 0.12.1 (not skipped) and t/07-testkit.t 68/68. No code touched; Primitives.pm left alone for the parallel agent.
